<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Nasir Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1310–1341</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Nasir Muhammad was a sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> whose main reign lasted from 1310 to 1341. Under him the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> state reached its institutional apex, with systematic allocation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iqta">iqta</a> land grants, administrative reforms and extensive building in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>. His long reign is often seen as the high point of Mamluk power and prosperity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-nasir-muhammad.jpg" alt="al-Nasir Muhammad" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 14th century authors · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maqamat_of_al-Hariri._Enthroned_Prince._Probably_Egypt_1334.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
